The land area of Italy is composed of forest, grasslands (including agricultural fields), built-up areas (for example towns and cities) and inland water bodies like lakes and rivers.

Table 5.1 shows changes in the area covered by these environments over a fifteen year period.

{{figure:reviewed_table_1.png}}

parts.text:
The increase in area covered by forest in Italy has occurred because farmers have cultivated less of their land or have abandoned their farms altogether.

Describe how this change in land use may affect biodiversity. You should consider the three different levels of biodiversity in your answer.

{{figure:reviewed_response_2.png}}
